-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1714,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><br></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(III)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">त्रिकोणीय पिरैमिडी</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(D)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.318ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1908.6 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1505,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><br></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(IV)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">त्रिकोणीय द्विपैरैमिडी</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></p>\n<p>नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सही उत्तर चुनें:</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>सूची I में दिए गए अणुओं को सूची II में उनकी संगत आकृतियों से मिलाने के लिए, हमें इलेक्ट्रॉनिक ज्यामिति और VSEPR (वैलेंस शेल इलेक्ट्रॉन पेयर रिपल्शन) सिद्धांत पर विचार करने की आवश्यकता है। यहाँ विस्तृत विश्लेषण दिया गया है:</p>\n\n<p><b><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (अमोनिया)</b>: अमोनिया में एक केंद्रीय नाइट्रोजन परमाणु होता है जो तीन हाइड्रोजन परमाणुओं से बंधित है और इसमें इलेक्ट्रॉनों का एक एकाकी युग्म है। इससे त्रिकोणीय पिरामिडी आकृति बनती है।</p>\n\n<p><b><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.954ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 2189.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"46\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-46\" transform=\"translate(1100,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1786,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (ब्रोमीन पेंटाफ्लोराइड)</b>: ब्रोमीन पेंटाफ्लोराइड में एक केंद्रीय ब्रोमीन परमाणु होता है जो पाँच फ्लोरीन परमाणुओं से बंधित है और इसमें इलेक्ट्रॉनों का एक एकाकी युग्म है। इससे वर्ग पिरामिडी आकृति बनती है।</p>\n\n<p><b><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.791ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2117.6 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"50\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-50\"></use><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\" transform=\"translate(681,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(1403,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1714,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (फॉस्फोरस पेंटाक्लोराइड)</b>: फॉस्फोरस पेंटाक्लोराइड में एक केंद्रीय फॉस्फोरस परमाणु होता है जो पाँच क्लोरीन परमाणुओं से बंधित है और कोई एकाकी युग्म नहीं है। इसके परिणामस्वरूप त्रिकोणीय द्विपिरामिडी आकृति बनती है।</p>\n\n<p><b><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.318ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1908.6 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1505,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (मीथेन)</b>: मीथेन में एक केंद्रीय कार्बन परमाणु होता है जो चार हाइड्रोजन परमाणुओं से बंधित है और कोई एकाकी युग्म नहीं है, जो एक चतुष्फलकीय संरचना बनाता है।</p>\n\n<p>उपरोक्त विश्लेषणों का उपयोग करते हुए, हम अणुओं और आकृतियों का मिलान निम्नानुसार कर सकते हैं:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>A (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) - III (त्रिकोणीय पिरामिडी)</li>\n\n<li>B (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.954ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 2189.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"46\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-46\" transform=\"translate(1100,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1786,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) - I (वर्ग पिरामिड)</li>\n\n<li>C (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.791ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2117.6 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"50\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-50\"></use><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\" transform=\"translate(681,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(1403,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1714,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) - IV (त्रिकोणीय द्विपिरामिडी)</li>\n\n<li>D (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.318ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1908.6 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1505,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) - II (चतुष्फलकीय)</li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<p>इसलिए, सही मिलान विकल्प B है:</p>\n\n<p><b>विकल्प B: A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II</b></p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"hybridization-and-vsepr-theory","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["matching_table"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-8th-april-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>To match the molecules in List I with their corresponding shapes in List II, we need to consider the electronic geometry and the VSEPR (Valence Shell Electron Pair Repulsion) theory. Here’s the detailed analysis:</p>\n\n<p><b><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Ammonia)</b>: Ammonia has a central nitrogen atom bonded to three hydrogen atoms and has one lone pair of electrons. This leads to a trigonal pyramidal shape.</p>\n\n<p><b><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.954ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 2189.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"46\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-46\" transform=\"translate(1100,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1786,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Bromine pentafluoride)</b>: Bromine pentafluoride has a central bromine atom bonded to five fluorine atoms and has one lone pair of electrons. This leads to a square pyramidal shape.</p>\n\n<p><b><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.791ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2117.6 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"50\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-50\"></use><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\" transform=\"translate(681,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(1403,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1714,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Phosphorus pentachloride)</b>: Phosphorus pentachloride has a central phosphorus atom bonded to five chlorine atoms and no lone pairs. This results in a trigonal bipyramidal shape.</p>\n\n<p><b><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.318ex\" height=\"1.934ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1908.6 855\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1505,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Methane)</b>: Methane has a central carbon atom bonded to four hydrogen atoms with no lone pairs, forming a tetrahedral structure.</p>\n\n<p>Using the above analyses, we can match the molecules and shapes as follows:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li>A (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1936.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1533,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) - III (Trigonal pyramidal)</li>\n\n<li>B (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=